(Q2) A binary isn’t found in $PATH. How would you use commands (which, find, locate) to troubleshoot and fix the issue?
  
FIND:

  # Search entire system (may be slow)
sudo find / -name "binary_name" -type f 2>/dev/null

# Search common locations first
find /usr/bin /usr/local/bin /opt /home -name "binary_name" -type f 2>/dev/null

# Search with wildcards if unsure of exact name
find / -name "*binary_name*" -type f 2>/dev/null

LOCATE:
  
# Update the database first (may need sudo)
sudo updatedb

# Search for the binary
locate binary_name

# Case-insensitive search
locate -i binary_name


