(Q7) Differentiate application, system and utility software in the context of Linux environment.
 Linux Software Classification: Application, System, and Utility Software
1. Application Software
Definition: End-user programs designed to accomplish specific tasks or solve particular problems for users.
Characteristics:
    • User-facing: Direct interaction with end users 
    • Task-specific: Designed for particular activities or workflows 
    • Independent operation: Can run without deep system integration 
    • Optional: Not required for basic system operation 
