Installation Locations:
    • /usr/bin/ - User binaries 
    • /usr/local/bin/ - Locally installed applications 
    • /opt/ - Optional/third-party applications 
    • ~/.local/bin/ - User-specific applications 

2. System Software
Definition: Core software that manages hardware resources and provides a platform for other software to run.
Characteristics:
    • Hardware interface: Direct interaction with hardware components 
    • Resource management: Controls CPU, memory, I/O devices 
    • Essential: Required for system operation 
    • Background operation: Usually runs without direct user interaction 
